# Pinned from the real red run of 2026-07-28 with the injection applied.
#
# The injection makes the classifier excuse a failure by NAME alone — it stops
# reading the registered signature. That is not a hypothetical regression: it is
# the exact behaviour this task was filed to delete. Classifying from the name
# is what a human does from memory, and it is how one failure got filed against
# TASK-5HBST when the mode that fired belonged to TASK-STWVB.
#
# Everything else about the runner still works under the injection — it runs,
# reruns failures in isolation, prints a verdict block, exits 0. A green
# classifier that has quietly stopped discriminating is indistinguishable from a
# working one, which is why the proof is pinned rather than re-authored.
exit: 1

# The mislabel detector itself: a registered name whose panic does not match the
# registered signature must be REAL. Under the injection it is waved through as
# a FLAKE and the run exits 0.
contains: FAIL registered name, WRONG signature -> REAL, exit 1 (the mislabel detector)

# The same defect from the other side: when one test name carries two entries
# with two owners, name-only matching picks whichever was written first and
# names the wrong task.
contains: FAIL two entries for one name -> the matching one wins and names its own owner

# Exactly two cases fall, and thirteen still pass. If a future edit makes the
# whole self-test collapse, that is a different failure and this proof has not
# reproduced the defect it claims to.
contains: 13 passed, 2 failed
